# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your real values.
# .env.local is already gitignored (see .env*.local in .gitignore) so your
# project ID/token never gets committed.
#
# HOW TO GET THESE VALUES:
# 1. Go to https://www.sanity.io/manage and create a free account (or log in).
# 2. Create a new project (any name, e.g. "Touchdown Freediving").
# 3. Once created, your Project ID is shown right on the project dashboard —
#    copy it into NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID below.
# 4. Leave the dataset as "production" unless you changed it when creating
#    the project.
# 5. Save this file as .env.local, then run: npm run dev
# 6. Visit http://localhost:3000/studio — that's your CMS. Log in with the
#    same account you used at sanity.io.
#
# Until these are filled in, the site keeps working exactly as it does today
# using the hardcoded content baked into lib/content.ts — nothing breaks.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
